terms=f'''{draft}<p>Version: {e(c['termsVersion'])}</p><h2>About this website</h2><p>This website introduces Eleven Forward, its mission, and products in development. The website operator is {e(business)}. Questions about these terms can be sent to {contacttext}.</p><h2>Products in development</h2><p>P001 is a prototype. Product and apparel images identified as concepts illustrate a design direction. Designs and details may change. This website does not accept orders, payments, or reservations, and it does not promise a release date.</p><h2>Email updates and consent</h2><p>Signing up means you agree to these terms and consent to receive Eleven Forward product updates and exclusive deals by email. Signup is voluntary. You can withdraw consent through the public contact email listed above. Withdrawal requests will be recorded and honored before further marketing is sent.</p><h2>Website content</h2><p>Eleven Forward branding and original website materials belong to their respective rights holders. You may view this website for personal use. Contact us for permission to reproduce brand artwork or other materials.</p><h2>Information and availability</h2><p>Website content describes our brand and development intentions. It is not individualized medical advice. We aim to keep information accurate, but content and site availability may change.</p><h2>Changes and contact</h2><p>When these terms change, we will publish an updated version on this page. Material changes to the use of signup information will be communicated as appropriate. Contact: {contacttext}.</p>'''
privacy=f'''{draft}<p>Version: {e(c['privacyVersion'])}</p><h2>Who operates this website</h2><p>The website operator is {e(business)}. Privacy questions and withdrawal requests can be sent to {contacttext}.</p><h2>Information submitted with signup</h2><p>If you choose to sign up, the form sends your email address, selected product interests when using the product form, consent choice, the consent wording and policy versions, and a fixed website source identifier. When JavaScript is available, it also sends a client-provided submission time. That time is not independently verified. We do not ask for your health information.</p><h2>How signup information is used</h2><p>We use signup information to provide product updates and exclusive deals and to keep a record of the consent associated with your signup. Signing up does not require you to share your ostomy status or any other health details.</p><h2>Service providers</h2><p>Cloudflare hosts this website and may process technical request information to deliver and protect it. Form submissions are sent to Web3Forms and delivered to the designated Eleven Forward inbox. Web3Forms and the inbox provider process information needed to handle and deliver those submissions. Their own privacy notices describe their processing practices.</p><h2>Cookies and tracking</h2><p>This release does not add analytics, advertising trackers, or marketing cookies. Hosting and form providers may process technical information for service delivery and security.</p><h2>Retention</h2><p><strong>[Owner must approve a retention schedule before launch.]</strong> Signup records and consent evidence are stored in the designated inbox. The retention schedule must address active signup records, withdrawal requests, and the minimum information retained to prevent further marketing after withdrawal.</p><h2>Withdrawing consent and privacy requests</h2><p>You can request withdrawal, access, correction, or deletion by emailing {contacttext}. We will handle requests according to applicable requirements. A minimal suppression record may be retained to honor a request not to receive further marketing. Marketing campaigns must include a working unsubscribe process before campaign sending begins.</p><h2>Changes</h2><p>Updates to this policy will be published here with a new version identifier. We will communicate material changes as appropriate.</p>'''
